[h2]Sector Control[/h2]
Capture and hold sectors to score points for your side. Holding more sectors raises the scoring rate. The first side to 100 points wins. You can return through eligible captured sectors, groupmates and mobile respawn vehicles.

[h2]On the battlefield[/h2]
[list]
[*]Use the group menu to organize players and AI. AI groups attack and defend objectives and can use transport, ground vehicles and boats where available.
[*]Stabilize and revive downed teammates. You can also move injured teammates out of danger.
[*]Order eligible vehicles, use service points and harbors, and collect supply drops. Vehicle choices depend on the terrain and your rank.
[*]The HUD shows sector ownership, ticket rates and respawn information. Press [b]F2[/b] to toggle the HUD.
[/list]

[h2]Rank and perks[/h2]
Earn XP for capturing and contesting sectors, revives, eliminations and assists. Ranks open new weapons, gear and vehicles. Use the Arsenal to build and save loadouts from the equipment you have unlocked.
[list]
[*]Rank 1: Experience and Medic.
[*]Ranks 5, 7 and 10: Stamina, Marksman and Machinegunner.
[*]Ranks 15, 18 and 20: Launcher, Armor and Grenadier.
[*]Ranks 22 and 25: Explosives and Suppressor.
[/list]
Perk slots unlock at ranks 1, 6, 18, 35, 67 and 100.

[h2]Lobby parameters[/h2]
Choose the layout or let the game pick one. Random layouts can scale with player count. The host can set vehicle spawn rules and cooldown, sector messages, thermal vision, launcher and high-caliber damage, progression storage, third-person view, weather, night skip and time multipliers.

[h2]Start the scenario[/h2]
Host the scenario in multiplayer and open Parameters in the lobby. The Chernarus 2020 edition requires the CUP addons listed on that Workshop page.

